    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy focus on exploiting the favorable matchups against Mike Burrows and Eric Lauer. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the charge with a 74.56 score, buoyed by a substantial 17% boost from the opposing SP skill profile and a 14% platoon advantage, making him our highest-rated start. **Jackson Merrill** also provides a significant ceiling at 72.26; his inclusion is critical not just for his offensive profile, but for his opportunistic base-running potential against a slower delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational priority on stolen bases. **Kyle Tucker** and **Cole Carrigg** round out a high-floor outfield, with **Cole Carrigg** specifically benefiting from a generous 5.28 xERA matchup against Eric Lauer, projecting as an elite play despite the volatility of the lower end of the order.\n\nWhile our core remains strong, the decision to slot **Heliot Ramos** into the UTIL spot represents our tightest margin. His 52.59 score reflects the difficulty of facing a high-caliber arm like Kevin Gausman, though he holds onto the spot largely due to his propensity for swiping bags against slow-working pitchers. On the bench, we are currently navigating a depleted roster with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all unavailable due to IL stints or scheduled off-days. This lack of depth places a premium on our starting nine; we are keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 63.36 is predicated on an assumed leadoff role\u2014should the confirmed lineup push him down the order, his efficiency score will likely dip, though he remains our primary catcher option for the day. Managers should remain alert for any late-breaking weather patterns, particularly for games involving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**, where wind conditions are currently providing a slight, yet variable, lift to their respective power profiles.",
